    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rules with a points system, keeping each responsibility in its natural home.\n\n**`model/MembershipLevel.java`** \u2014 now the membership scoring authority:\n- `points(owner[, asOf])` \u2014 starts at 0 and adds `+2` for email, `+1` for zero namesakes, `+2` for a household of 3+ (`householdMemberCount >= 3`), `+3` for tenure over 365 days. Each factor is an independent named constant.\n- `level(points)` \u2014 pure mapping: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n- `of(owner)` \u2014 now just `level(points(owner))`, so the level always derives from the points rather than recomputing the factors. This preserves the existing call site in `AuditOwnerCreated`.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `membershipPoints` field and updated `membershipLevel` (now 1\u20134, described as derived from points) so the generated `OwnerDto` carries both.\n\n**`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `membershipPoints` mapping/helper alongside the existing `membershipLevel` one, both delegating to `MembershipLevel` (no duplicated rule logic).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest` (fresh owner with email, no namesake, single-member household, zero tenure \u2192 `membershipPoints=3`, `membershipLevel=2`) and the full suite pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
