    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered list of everything that happens on `POST /api/owners`.\n\n## Precondition (endpoint-wide)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 the whole file is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before any step runs.\n- **Transaction** \u2014 every step declares `govern: [ transaction ]`, so the entire pipeline runs in one write transaction that commits once at the end (or rolls back on any escalation).\n\nThe body is bound (`@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`) only at step 1 and republished as a variable; every later step reads/mutates that same instance via `@Val`.\n\n## The pipeline, in order\n\n1. **ValidateOwnerFields** *(validation)* \u2014 requires `firstName`, `lastName`, `address` (checked in its *normalized* form, so whitespace-only fails), `city`, and `telephone` to be present and non-blank. Reports **all** missing fields at once \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n\n2. **ValidateOwnerPostcode** *(validation)* \u2014 postcode is optional; if present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the city has a known region it must fall in that region's pinned range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Otherwise \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (400).\n\n3. **ValidateRegistrationDate** *(validation)* \u2014 registration date is optional; if supplied it must not be after the current server date (checked against the *raw* supplied value, before any business-day roll) \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n\n4. **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 rewrites `telephone` to canonical E.164 in place (strips spaces/dashes/brackets, assumes +61 and drops a leading 0 when no `+`, enforces national-number length for +61/+1). Unconvertible \u2192 `InvalidTelephoneException` (400).\n\n5. **NormalizeOwnerEmail** *(side-effect + validation)* \u2014 email is optional; absent/blank left untouched. If present, must be syntactically valid (\u2192 `InvalidEmailException`, 400), then stored back lower-cased.\n\n6. **RejectDisposableEmail** *(validation)* \u2014 if an email is present, its domain must not be a known disposable provider (mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com) \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400).\n\n7. **NormalizeOwnerAddress** *(side-effect)* \u2014 rewrites `address` in place to canonical form: trimmed, whitespace collapsed, upper-cased, and street-type abbreviations expanded (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n\n8. **EnsureUniqueHousehold** *(validation)* \u2014 unless the request sets `sharesHousehold=true`, rejects the create if any existing owner has the same household id (normalized last name + postcode) \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException`. Scans all owners.\n\n9. **EnsureCityCapacity** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects if the request's city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case/whitespace-insensitive city match) \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n10. **BuildOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 maps the (now-normalized) DTO to a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`, published for the remaining steps.\n\n11. **AssignHousehold** *(side-effect)* \u2014 stamps the owner's `householdId` (deterministic hash of last name + postcode).\n\n12. **DefaultRegistrationDate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if no registration date was supplied, sets it to today (server date).\n\n13. **RollRegistrationDateToBusinessDay** *(side-effect)* \u2014 if the (supplied or defaulted) date is a Saturday/Sunday, rolls it forward to the following Monday. This adjusted date drives the next two steps.\n\n14. **EnsureDailyLimit** *(validation)* \u2014 rejects if \u2265 100 owners already carry that (business-day) registration date \u2192 `DailyLimitReachedException`.\n\n15. **AssignCustomerCode** *(side-effect)* \u2014 sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>`, region derived from postcode/city plus a hash over the normalized telephone and last name (so it depends on step 4 having run).\n\n16. **CountNamesakes** *(side-effect)* \u2014 counts existing owners matching first+last name and stores it as `namesakeCount` (state just before this create).\n\n17. **CountHouseholdMembers** *(side-effect)* \u2014 counts existing owners in the same household and adds 1 for this owner, stored as `householdMemberCount` (minimum 1).\n\n18. **DetectPossibleDuplicate** *(side-effect)* \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold=true`, finds the earliest existing owner in the same household with a *different* telephone; sets `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (that owner's id, or null).\n\n19. **SaveOwner** *(side-effect)* \u2014 persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save`, generating its id.\n\n20. **AuditOwnerCreated** *(side-effect)* \u2014 logs an audit line to the `AUDIT` logger: id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n\n21. **RespondWithOwnerCreated** *(side-effect / response)* \u2014 maps the saved owner to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning=true` when > 80 owners share that day, and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n### Notes on ordering rationale (as the code enforces it)\n- All three pure validations that don't need the built entity (fields \u2192 postcode \u2192 registration-date) run first, so a bad body is a 400 before any mutation.\n- Telephone is normalized before the customer-code hash (step 15) and before duplicate detection (step 18) that compare on telephone.\n- The registration date is defaulted *then* rolled to a business day *before* the daily-limit check and before it's read by the response's bulk-signup warning \u2014 so both see the adjusted business-day date.\n- `sharesHousehold=true` bypasses only the hard household-uniqueness rejection (step 8) and the soft-duplicate flag (step 18); the household id/link and member count are still assigned unconditionally."
